nected  to that anymore now he just guards the  soul stone the only one of the six  Infinity stones that uses its owner  rather than letting its owner use it so  what's it all mean why would we see the  Red Skull in the scene at all well it  may be foreshadowing you know that there  are a lot of people who kick the bucket  in the end thanks to thanasis supreme  snap some of those people including  spider-man Doctor Strange and Black  Panther are expected to have more than  one stand-alone project on the MCU films  late so mourning those losses seems  premature to say the least  meanwhile the sole stone in the comics  tends to capture its wielder and contain  the souls of others within it in a place  called soul world so it's possible that  the red school wasn't trapped on war  mere to guard the stone instead he may  be one of the stones prisoners after all  the Red Skull has been there for decades  he should be dead but the soul stone has  kept him alive this whole time so maybe  some of the other characters who seemed  to die in infinity war have been kept  alive by the soul stone too  this could potentially answer the  question of how some of the many  superheroes who bit the dust in the film  could be brought back in time for the  4th movie could those who are snapped  out of existence all be residing in the  soul world now there are other ways the  4th Avengers film could bring back those  lost heroes of course especially since  the time stone was proven to be able to  do exactly that by Thanos himself but if  the Russo brothers are looking to  surprise some folks with a more  unexpected resurrection  well the red skulls guardianship of the  soul stone might have just laid the  groundwork for exactly that Wow thanks  for watching click the looper icon to  subscribe to our youtube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  you'll love to  [Music]
 

